  "schematicNotes": [
    {
      "id": "n_can",
      "width": 390,
      "text": "CAN BUS harness. 1 Mbit/s ISO 11898-2. Only the CAN-Lambda crosses the firewall, on bulkhead B c13 / c14 (CAN) and c3 / c4 (+12V / GND); the cluster and RealDash are CAN drops only - their devices and their power are not part of this harness. 120R termination at the ECU end and at the lambda end.",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3210,
        "y": -60
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_cavity_notes",
      "text": "CAVITY NOTES - full text of the signals marked * on this drawing\nLink CAN-Lambda c1: Power +12V ign, RFRM LAM 7.5A - broken off here, continues on ST185-B-engine, bulkhead B c3, ST185-B-cabin, from ST185-CabinPower fuse RFRM LAM\nt_cluster_can: TrackCluster ESP32-P4 - CAN drop (device not in this harness)\nt_realdash_can: RealDash Pi 5 - CAN drop (device not in this harness)\nsp_shield_can (Splice): CAN drain T-splice at the bus branch point (Daniel 2026-10-12). The trunk drain w_shd_can runs on (broken off) to ST185-B-cabin and is T-spliced there onto the B17 drain; each node branch drain (ECU port, CSB3, cluster, RealDash, bulkhead / Lambda) is soldered onto the trunk drain here where 6 mm of its insulation is cut away. Drains stay 20 AWG - no combined-gauge pigtail.",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 3210,
        "y": 150
      }
    }
  ],
